# Agent Guidelines

- Package management: `uv`
- Hooks: `prek install -t pre-commit -t commit-msg -t pre-push` then `prek run --all-files`
- Skill sync: `uv run library-skills --tool-skill install --claude --yes --all`
- Linting: `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run ruff format .`
- Type checking: `uv run pyright`
- Tests: `uv run pytest`
- Migrations: `uv run alembic upgrade head`
- Architecture: Configurable scopes with dependency injection, async SQLAlchemy, queue handoff{% if enable_telemetry %}, and OpenTelemetry{% endif %}
- `container.py` defines the `ServiceContainer` shape (no runtime service imports); `bootstrap.py` builds one. Don't import `bootstrap` from request-time code — import `container` instead.
- `azure-storage-queue` is optional (`uv sync --extra azure`); don't hard-import it at module scope in `database/queues.py`.
{% if enable_azure_auth -%}
- Azure Entra ID auth: `core/auth.py` builds `azure_scheme` (JWT validation) from the container's own settings, and `get_current_user` resolves the caller from it. Use `CurrentUserDep` for "any authenticated caller" and `require_role("X")` for app-role-gated routes. `require_role` wires `get_current_user` to the provider-agnostic `check_role(role, user)` (assumes only `user.roles`); a non-Entra provider later reuses `check_role` with its own identity dependency. Never hand-roll token parsing; never call `azure_scheme` with real tokens in tests — override `get_current_user` via `app.dependency_overrides` instead. Router-level `dependencies=[Depends(get_current_user)]` is what actually gates the example `/items` and `/tasks` routes — a new router needs the same treatment, or it stays unauthenticated even with `enable_azure_auth=true`.
{% endif -%}
